Package: rpyodide
Title: Call Python (Pyodide) from R in webR, Like 'reticulate'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("John", "Muschelli", , "muschellij2@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6469-1750"))
Description: A 'reticulate'-style interface for calling Python from R when R
    runs in the web browser through 'webR' (R compiled to WebAssembly). Python
    runs in 'Pyodide' (CPython compiled to WebAssembly) in its own web worker,
    and R talks to it synchronously through 'webR' worker messaging. Supports
    running code, importing modules, calling functions, converting vectors,
    lists, matrices and data frames to and from 'NumPy' and 'pandas',
    installing packages with 'micropip', and several independent Python
    sessions.
